***************************** T A L Y S **************************2931 1451  192
                                                                  2931 1451  193
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   2931 1451  194
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      2931 1451  195
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    2931 1451  196
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     2931 1451  197
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  2931 1451  198
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        2931 1451  199
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    2931 1451  200
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         2931 1451  201
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      2931 1451  202
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    2931 1451  203
stored in this data file:                                         2931 1451  204
                                                                  2931 1451  205
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   2931 1451  206
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     2931 1451  207
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 2931 1451  208
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   2931 1451  209
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                2931 1451  210
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   2931 1451  211
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    2931 1451  212
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        2931 1451  213
- Recoil data                                                     2931 1451  214
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           2931 1451  215
- Total particle energy spectra                                   2931 1451  216
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      2931 1451  217
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        2931 1451  218
- Residual production cross sections                              2931 1451  219
                                                                  2931 1451  220
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            2931 1451  221
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        2931 1451  222
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   2931 1451  223
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                2931 1451  224
                                                                  2931 1451  225
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************2931 1451  226
